cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GasBrineBench: a benchmark dataset of experimental gas-brine thermodynamic data"
abstract: >-
  A curated, quality-coded benchmark of experimental thermodynamic data for
  gas-brine systems: gas solubility, brine density, osmotic coefficients,
  vapor-pressure lowering, gas-phase water content, enthalpy of dissolution
  and brine permittivity, in single- and mixed-salt aqueous electrolyte
  solutions. 26,815 rows from 249 published sources in 11 families, covering
  seven benchmark gases (CO2, CH4, H2, N2, O2, C2H6, C3H8; 24 further gases
  are flagged) and six ions (Na+, K+, Ca2+, Mg2+, Cl-, SO4 2-) over 238-773 K
  and 0.1-3,500 bar, including a CO2 + CH4 + water ternary family, and a
  separate supplementary tier of 5,174 measurements that the benchmark
  families cannot hold. Every row carries its source, an R/T/U quality code
  with a documented justification, a fit/test tag and modifier flags; the
  tables the values were taken from are included.
message: >-
  The numerical values are measurements published by the authors cited in
  SOURCES.md; please cite those primary sources for the data you use, and
  this repository for the compilation. Cite the version DOI below, not the
  concept DOI: a benchmark result is only reproducible if it names the
  snapshot it was computed against. A data-descriptor reference will be
  added here if one is published.
type: dataset
version: 1.2.1
